
--- The methods a request may have (`spec/31 §1`, ADR 0123 rule 1). The host answers any other
--- with `501`.
pub kind Method = Get | Head | Post | Put | Patch | Delete | Options

--- One decoded query parameter of a request, as `name=value` (`spec/31 §4` rule 4).
pub kind Param
  name: internal Text
  value: internal Text

--- A request, as the host read it (`spec/31 §3`, `§4`): its target in origin-form as received,
--- its path split on `/` and percent-decoded segment by segment, the parameters of its query
--- decoded in order, its headers with names in ASCII lower case in the order received, its
--- whole body, the peer's IP address without its port, and the grant's address as the grant
--- writes it. The parameters are `params`, since `query` is a reserved word (`spec/01`).
pub kind Request
  method: internal Method
  target: internal Text
  segments: internal List[Text]
  params: internal List[Param]
  headers: internal List[Header]
  body: internal Text
  peer: internal Text
  listener: internal Text

--- A request and the reply right to answer it once (`spec/31 §1`, ADR 0123 rule 4).
pub kind Exchange
  request: internal Request
  right: internal ReplyRight

--- The status of a reply: a `1xx` status is the host's alone (`spec/31 §5`).
pub kind Status = Int where 200 <= it and it <= 599

--- A reply to a request (`spec/31 §5`): the host writes its framing headers itself.
pub kind Reply
  status: internal Status
  headers: internal List[Header]
  body: internal Text

--- Why an operation of `HttpServer` fails (`spec/31 §1`): `Interrupted` at a host stop,
--- `TimedOut` when a deadline of the program cuts the wait of `next`, `Closed` after `close`,
--- `NotHeld` for a reply right the task does not hold or answered already, and `BadReply` for
--- a reply the host refuses to send.
pub kind ServeError = Interrupted | TimedOut | Closed | NotHeld | BadReply

--- The server side of HTTP/1.1, on the addresses that `serve` grants allow (`spec/31 §1`, ADR
--- 0123 rules 1 to 5). `next` waits for a request and gives the calling task its reply right;
--- `reply` answers it once and never waits; `close` stops accepting connections, and accepts
--- `public` only, so no request decides it.
pub capability HttpServer
  op next() -> internal Exchange
    fails ServeError
    accepts internal
  op reply(to: ReplyRight, reply: Reply) -> Unit
    fails ServeError
    accepts internal
  op close() -> Unit
    accepts public
